  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "The mean age of Amanda’s \\(4\\) cousins is \\(8,\\) and their median age is \\(5.\\) What is the sum of the ages of Amanda’s youngest and oldest cousins?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\ 13 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\ 16 \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\ 19 \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\ 22 \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\ 25 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Let the ages in increasing order be \\(a\\le b\\le c\\le d\\). The mean determines their total:\n\\[\na+b+c+d=4\\cdot8=32.\n\\]\nFor four ages, the median is the average of the middle two. Thus\n\\[\n\\frac{b+c}{2}=5,\n\\qquad b+c=10.\n\\]\nRemoving these middle ages from the total leaves the youngest and oldest:\n\\[\na+d=32-10=22.\n\\]\nTheir ages sum to \\(22\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
